 This repository holds only what is ard's: the `Makefile` targets CI runs, `Dockerfile`, `deploy/` and `deploy/cosign.pub`, the key ard images are signed with. `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, `deploy/` and any `Jenkinsfile*` are in ard's `merge.protected_paths`, so the merger never lands a change to them without a human approva\n\n- **Checks.** The Jenkins multibranch job `ard-ci` builds every same-repository branch and pull request, `worker/*` branches included, but never forks, with `make lint`, `make test`, `make build` and `make chart-test`. Its pipeline is loaded from the deployment repository, never from the branch, so branch code supplies only those targets and runs in a pod with no credential and no service account token. `main` requires both its status, `continuous-integration/jenkins/pr-merge`, and the Actions `test` job ([#219](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/219)): Jenkins stops reporting to a PR \n- **Publish.** A green `main` build starts `ard-build`, whose Jenkinsfile is not in this repository, so nothing merged here can reach its credentials. It builds the `Dockerfile` for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64` (no emulation: every `RUN` cross-compiles or downloads on the build platform), signs the digest with cosign, and pushes `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard:sha-<7>` (never re-pushed) and `:main`.\n- **Deploy.** A deploy job verifies the signature and the revision label, checks the new commit descends from the pinned one, and pins the digest and commit in the deployment repository. Argo CD renders this repository's `deploy/argocd` chart (the app of apps) with that pin and the site's values: one child Application per target repository, named `ard-<instance>`, reading `deploy/charts/ard-serve` at the pinned commit, so chart and image move together. The cluster admits no other Application from that chart.\n- **Release.** An annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` (`git tag -a`) builds that commit with `VERSION=vX.Y.Z`, pushes `:vX.Y.Z` and moves `:latest` when it is the highest version. Release tags are annotated because Jenkins builds only tags at most a day old and dates a lightweight tag by its commit, so a lightweight tag on an older commit never builds. Releases do not change what is deployed, which follows `main`.\n- **Kill switch in a cluster.** `kubectl -n <namespace> exec deploy/ard-<instance> -- touch /home/ard/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` pauses `ard serve`; `rm` resumes.\n\n# Layout\n\nEvery top-level directory and Go package, with what it holds. Keep it current: a PR that adds, removes or renames a directory or package updates this file in the same PR.\n\n```\ncmd/ard/                    CLI entry point; wire a new subcommand by adding one line to handlers()\ninternal/cli/               cobra command tree, global flags, slog logging; Handlers is the plug-in point\ninternal/botcheck/          tests for the bot-commit audit in .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\ninternal/github/            GitHub client: domain types, Reader/Writer/Client, App auth, retry transport; query/ (search builder), fake/ (test double), clienttest/ (conformance suite)\ninternal/config/            .ard/config.yaml + role directory loading into a Resolved value (pure, fs.FS in)\ninternal/configcmd/         `ard config check` handler: prints the resolved config, returns validation errors; `--ref` checks a commit\ninternal/configsrc/         config from origin/main: a snapshot per SHA under ~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/ (what `ard serve` reads)\n# Gate 2 runbook: first loop proven (#39)\n\nGate 2 proves triage, worker and review on real issues before the merger takes\nover. ard runs live with the local executor on the owner's Mac, and a human\nmerges every PR. See [docs/proposal.md: Rollout](../proposal.md#rollout).\n\n**Done when** (from #39):","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"134331be-a9b3-411a-a3cb-0c7c0e56132c","uuid":"a72f04d4-3afb-407d-82c4-7123e59ed93c","timestamp":"2026-11-24T13:00:44.721Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":